2026-09-02 11:36:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] can help ensure the sampling remains fast and deterministic:
2026-09-02 11:36:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-09-02 11:36:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] 1. Buffer Architecture (Fixed-Size Ring Buffer)
2026-09-02 11:36:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Pre-allocation: Dynamic containers like `std::vector` or `std::queue` can trigger heap
2026-09-02 11:36:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] reallocations during runtime, which introduces non-deterministic delays. A pre-allocated circular
2026-09-02 11:36:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] buffer (ring buffer) avoids dynamic memory overhead.
2026-09-02 11:36:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Element Layout: Storing the sample as a pair of 32-bit unsigned integers (`timestamp` and
2026-09-02 11:36:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] `pins`) creates an 8-byte record, fitting cleanly into standard alignment boundaries.
2026-09-02 11:36:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-09-02 11:36:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] 2. Timing and Polling Latency
2026-09-02 11:36:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] • `sleep_us(100)` Impact: Sleeping for 100 microseconds inside the change-detection loop
2026-09-02 11:36:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] limits the maximum sampling frequency to roughly 10 kHz. For fast bus transactions (such as ROM
2026-09-02 11:36:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] accesses, which often complete in tens to hundreds of nanoseconds), polling without delay, using
2026-09-02 11:36:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] GPIO interrupt handlers, or using the RP2040 PIO (Programmable I/O) hardware will yield
2026-09-02 11:36:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] significantly higher fidelity.
2026-09-02 11:36:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Timestamp Rollover: A 32-bit microsecond counter (`t32`) overflows after approximately
2026-09-02 11:36:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] 71.58 minutes. If long captures are required, either store the full 64-bit timestamp or handle the
2026-09-02 11:36:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] 32-bit delta rollover in the consumer logic.
2026-09-02 11:36:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-09-02 11:36:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] 3. Concurrency and Data Transfer
2026-09-02 11:36:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Lock-Free Sharing: If one core captures the pin states while the other core processes or
2026-09-02 11:36:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] transmits the buffer, a single-producer single-consumer (SPSC) lock-free ring buffer using atomic
2026-09-02 11:36:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] head and tail pointers avoids mutex contention.
2026-09-02 11:36:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Overflow Handling: Decide whether new samples should be dropped or if older unread
2026-09-02 11:36:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] samples should be overwritten when the buffer reaches capacity.
