2026-09-03 17:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] The disconnection of COM6 during a trace dump is most likely caused by the hardware watchdog
2026-09-03 17:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] timer expiring and resetting the RP2040.
2026-09-03 17:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-03 17:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] Here is an analysis of why this occurs and other contributing factors:
2026-09-03 17:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-03 17:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-03 17:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-03 17:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 1. Watchdog Starvation During Trace Transmission (Primary Cause)
2026-09-03 17:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] • In `runShell()`, the hardware watchdog is enabled with a 1200&nbsp;ms timeout:
2026-09-03 17:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-03 17:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash]   watchdog_enable(WatchdogTimeout, false); // WatchdogTimeout = 1200 ms
2026-09-03 17:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-03 17:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] • In `sampleRom()`, the function captures the trace and then iterates through `pinBuffer` to
2026-09-03 17:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] transmit every sample:
2026-09-03 17:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash]   * Over 500 samples are transmitted (`id: 200001` through `id: 200513`).
2026-09-03 17:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash]   * Each iteration performs string formatting, invokes `rpcSend()`, calls `cdcFlush()`, and calls
2026-09-03 17:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] `tud_task()`.
2026-09-03 17:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash]   * Over USB Full-Speed CDC (1&nbsp;ms frame intervals), sending 500+ separate JSON-RPC packets
2026-09-03 17:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] with individual flushes typically takes between 1.0 and 1.5 seconds.
2026-09-03 17:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] • `watchdog_update()` is not called anywhere inside `sampleRom()` (neither in the capture
2026-09-03 17:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] loop nor in the transmission loop). Once the cumulative time exceeds 1200&nbsp;ms, the watchdog
2026-09-03 17:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] resets the processor. The USB connection drops immediately, which Windows reports as COM6
2026-09-03 17:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] disconnecting.
2026-09-03 17:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-03 17:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-03 17:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-03 17:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 2. USB Task Starvation During the Capture Loop
2026-09-03 17:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] • While waiting for bus state changes inside the capture loop (`while ((pins & enable) == 0)`),
2026-09-03 17:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] `sleep_us(100)` is called without invoking `tud_task()`.
2026-09-03 17:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] • If a burst capture runs long enough without servicing TinyUSB, the host USB stack may register an
2026-09-03 17:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] endpoint timeout or transaction failure before transmission even completes.
2026-09-03 17:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-03 17:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-03 17:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-03 17:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 3. Per-Line CDC Flush Overhead
2026-09-03 17:32:24 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Calling `cdcFlush()` on every single sample forces the USB driver to try to push individual
2026-09-03 17:32:24 [gemini-3.8-flash] packets rather than batching CDC data into full 64-byte USB packets.
2026-09-03 17:32:24 [gemini-3.8-flash] • This drastically reduces throughput, prolongs the time spent inside the transmit loop, and
2026-09-03 17:32:24 [gemini-3.8-flash] increases the likelihood of tripping the watchdog timer.
2026-09-03 17:32:24 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-03 17:32:24 [gemini-3.8-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-03 17:32:24 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-03 17:32:24 [gemini-3.8-flash] 4. Dynamic Vector Allocation
2026-09-03 17:32:24 [gemini-3.8-flash] • `pinBuffer.push_back(...)` is called dynamically without `pinBuffer.reserve()`. Repeated heap
2026-09-03 17:32:24 [gemini-3.8-flash] reallocations on an embedded micro-controller can cause execution jitter and memory fragmentation,
2026-09-03 17:32:24 [gemini-3.8-flash] although the watchdog reset during transmission is the immediate failure mechanism here.
2026-09-03 17:32:24 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-03 17:32:24 [gemini-3.8-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-03 17:32:24 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-03 17:32:24 [gemini-3.8-flash] Suggested Resolutions
2026-09-03 17:32:24 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-03 17:32:24 [gemini-3.8-flash] 1. Feed the Watchdog During Dump:
2026-09-03 17:32:24 [gemini-3.8-flash]    Add a call to `watchdog_update()` inside the sample transmission loop in `sampleRom()` (and
2026-09-03 17:32:24 [gemini-3.8-flash] optionally inside the sampling wait loop if sample windows can exceed a few hundred milliseconds).
