2026-09-04 10:38:44 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-09-04 10:38:44 [glm-5.3-flash] `tud_cdc_write` returns 0 when the TX ring is full. If the host stops reading (window stalled,
2026-09-04 10:38:44 [glm-5.3-flash] cable swapped to a slow hub, DTR glitch) this spins forever with no watchdog_update within reach —
2026-09-04 10:38:44 [glm-5.3-flash] a 1200 ms timeout is one hung flush away from a mid-capture reboot. Escape hatch:
2026-09-04 10:38:44 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-09-04 10:38:44 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-09-04 10:38:44 [glm-5.3-flash] void writeCDC(const char* str,size_t charCount){
2026-09-04 10:38:44 [glm-5.3-flash] 	if(!tud_cdc_connected()){
2026-09-04 10:38:44 [glm-5.3-flash] 		return;
2026-09-04 10:38:44 [glm-5.3-flash] 	}
2026-09-04 10:38:44 [glm-5.3-flash] 	size_t writePos=0;
2026-09-04 10:38:44 [glm-5.3-flash] 	int stallCount=0;
2026-09-04 10:38:44 [glm-5.3-flash] 	while(writePos<charCount){
2026-09-04 10:38:44 [glm-5.3-flash] 		uint32_t writeCount=tud_cdc_write(str+writePos,charCount-writePos);
2026-09-04 10:38:44 [glm-5.3-flash] 		if(writeCount==0){
2026-09-04 10:38:44 [glm-5.3-flash] 			if(!tud_cdc_connected()||++stallCount>1000){
2026-09-04 10:38:44 [glm-5.3-flash] 				break;	// host gone or not draining: drop the remainder
2026-09-04 10:38:44 [glm-5.3-flash] 			}
2026-09-04 10:38:44 [glm-5.3-flash] 			tud_cdc_write_flush();
2026-09-04 10:38:44 [glm-5.3-flash] 			continue;
2026-09-04 10:38:44 [glm-5.3-flash] 		}
2026-09-04 10:38:44 [glm-5.3-flash] 		stallCount=0;
2026-09-04 10:38:44 [glm-5.3-flash] 		writePos+=writeCount;
2026-09-04 10:38:44 [glm-5.3-flash] 	}
2026-09-04 10:38:44 [glm-5.3-flash] 	tud_cdc_write_flush();
2026-09-04 10:38:44 [glm-5.3-flash] }
