2026-09-04 14:22:12 [grok-build-0.1] characters like `\n`, `\t`, `\"`, `\\`, etc. into their escaped form (i.e. turning an actual
2026-09-04 14:22:12 [grok-build-0.1] newline into the two characters `\` and `n`).
