2026-09-05 10:30:20 [grok-build-0.1] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.2 grok-build-0.1 𝕏 🪠 0.7° $0.007 17.00KB 6.25s
2026-09-05 10:30:20 [grok-build-0.1] .tscn stands for Text Scene.
2026-09-05 10:30:20 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 10:30:20 [grok-build-0.1] Breakdown:
2026-09-05 10:30:20 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 10:30:20 [grok-build-0.1] ╭─────────────┬────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
2026-09-05 10:30:20 [grok-build-0.1] │  Extension  │  Full Name         │  Meaning                                       │
2026-09-05 10:30:20 [grok-build-0.1] ├─────────────┼────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
2026-09-05 10:30:20 [grok-build-0.1] │  `.tscn`    │  **Text Scene**    │  Human-readable scene file                     │
2026-09-05 10:30:20 [grok-build-0.1] │  `.scn`     │  Binary Scene      │  Compiled/binary version of a scene            │
2026-09-05 10:30:20 [grok-build-0.1] │  `.tres`    │  Text Resource     │  Human-readable resource file                  │
2026-09-05 10:30:20 [grok-build-0.1] │  `.res`     │  Binary Resource   │  Compiled/binary resource                      │
2026-09-05 10:30:20 [grok-build-0.1] ╰─────────────┴────────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
2026-09-05 10:30:20 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 10:30:20 [grok-build-0.1] Simple explanation:
2026-09-05 10:30:20 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 10:30:20 [grok-build-0.1] - A `.tscn` file contains all the nodes, properties, and connections of a scene in plain text.
2026-09-05 10:30:20 [grok-build-0.1] - Godot saves scenes as `.tscn` by default so they are easy to read, edit, and version control
2026-09-05 10:30:20 [grok-build-0.1] (with Git, for example).
2026-09-05 10:30:20 [grok-build-0.1] - You can open a `.tscn` file in any text editor and see what's inside.
2026-09-05 10:30:20 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 10:30:20 [grok-build-0.1] Example from your project:
2026-09-05 10:30:20 [grok-build-0.1] Your `control.tscn` is a text scene that describes your `Control` node and attaches `control.gd` to
2026-09-05 10:30:20 [grok-build-0.1] it.
2026-09-05 10:30:20 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 10:30:20 [grok-build-0.1] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-05 10:30:20 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 10:30:20 [grok-build-0.1] Would you like to see what the inside of a `.tscn` file actually represents?
2026-09-05 10:30:20 [grok-build-0.1] 
