2026-09-05 10:56:10 [grok-build-0.1] How to regenerate a checksum in this project
2026-09-05 10:56:10 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 10:56:10 [grok-build-0.1] Godot stores checksums/hashes in two main places:
2026-09-05 10:56:10 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 10:56:10 [grok-build-0.1] 1. `.import` files (for assets like your `icon.svg`)
2026-09-05 10:56:10 [grok-build-0.1] 2. `.uid` files (for scripts and scenes)
2026-09-05 10:56:10 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 10:56:10 [grok-build-0.1] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-05 10:56:10 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 10:56:10 [grok-build-0.1] Best way (Recommended)
2026-09-05 10:56:10 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 10:56:10 [grok-build-0.1] 1. Open the project in the Godot editor.
2026-09-05 10:56:10 [grok-build-0.1] 2. In the FileSystem dock, find the source file (e.g. `icon.svg` or any `.glb`).
2026-09-05 10:56:10 [grok-build-0.1] 3. Right-click it → Reimport.
2026-09-05 10:56:10 [grok-build-0.1] 4. Godot will delete the old cached version and generate a fresh checksum + import file.
2026-09-05 10:56:11 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 10:56:11 [grok-build-0.1] You can also force a full regeneration by:
2026-09-05 10:56:11 [grok-build-0.1] - Deleting the `.import` file (e.g. `icon.svg.import`)
2026-09-05 10:56:11 [grok-build-0.1] - Deleting the corresponding file inside `.godot/imported/`
2026-09-05 10:56:11 [grok-build-0.1] - Then reimporting
2026-09-05 10:56:11 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 10:56:11 [grok-build-0.1] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-05 10:56:11 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 10:56:11 [grok-build-0.1] If you want to do it without the editor
2026-09-05 10:56:11 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 10:56:11 [grok-build-0.1] Tell me which file you want the checksum regenerated for, and paste the current content (or
2026-09-05 10:56:11 [grok-build-0.1] the base64 if it's binary).
2026-09-05 10:56:11 [grok-build-0.1] 
