2026-09-05 11:20:51 [grok-build-0.1] Here are the things I think are currently most important to consider, ranked roughly by impact:
2026-09-05 11:20:51 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:20:51 [grok-build-0.1] 1. Root Node Choice (Very Important Right Now)
2026-09-05 11:20:51 [grok-build-0.1] Your current root is a `Control`. This is fine for pure UI and logging, but it creates friction the
2026-09-05 11:20:51 [grok-build-0.1] moment you want to spawn 3D content (GLBs).
2026-09-05 11:20:51 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:20:51 [grok-build-0.1] - 3D nodes added under a `Control` will not render by default.
2026-09-05 11:20:51 [grok-build-0.1] - You will need some kind of bridge (SubViewport, separate 3D scene, or changing the root
2026-09-05 11:20:51 [grok-build-0.1] structure) to actually see the models.
2026-09-05 11:20:51 [grok-build-0.1] - This decision affects how clean your scene hierarchy stays as the project grows.
2026-09-05 11:20:51 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:20:51 [grok-build-0.1] • Question: How important is it that you can see* the spawned GLBs in the near
2026-09-05 11:20:51 [grok-build-0.1] future?
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] 2. Logging Discipline
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] You've already run into output overflow and connection drops caused by excessive logging.
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] Even if it feels harmless now, logging every incoming message (especially high-frequency ones like
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] `tick`) becomes a serious liability. It affects:
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] - Performance
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] - Readability of logs
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] - Connection stability
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] This is one of the easiest things to get wrong early.
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] 3. Message Semantics (Request vs Notification)
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] You're using JSON-RPC, but not all messages need a response.
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] - `tick` looks like a heartbeat or state update. Does it really need any reply?
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] - `spawn` probably does need some form of feedback (success/failure).
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] - Over-responding creates noise and potential loops.
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] Think about which messages are commands vs state updates.
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] 4. Connection Reality vs Intent
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] Your script still tries to connect upstream to port 9000 on every run, even though nothing appears
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] to be there.
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] This raises a bigger question:
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] - Is the Godot side meant to be a client to something else (port 9000), or purely a
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] server for the TypeScript client?
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] - The current dual role (listening + connecting upstream) adds complexity and failure points.
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] 5. Separation of Concerns
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] Right now most logic lives in one `Node`. As you add spawning, different GLB handling, state
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] tracking, etc., this can get messy quickly.
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] Worth thinking about early:
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] - Should networking stay isolated from scene creation?
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] - Do you want a central "command handler" or should things be more event-driven?
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] 6. Reliability Expectations
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] You asked about checksums and ACKs earlier. This is important to decide on now rather than later:
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] - Are `tick` messages allowed to be lost?
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] - Do `spawn` commands need guaranteed delivery or at least confirmation?
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] - How much do you care about message ordering?
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:20:52 [grok-build-0.1] WebSocket + JSON-RPC gives you very little of this for free.
