2026-09-05 11:34:55 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:34:55 [grok-build-0.1] Questions that would help clarify priorities:
2026-09-05 11:34:55 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:34:55 [grok-build-0.1] 1. Do you want the display to look authentic (with some softness/glow), or as clean and
2026-09-05 11:34:55 [grok-build-0.1] sharp as possible?
2026-09-05 11:34:55 [grok-build-0.1] 2. Will the 6502 simulator be sending line data in batches, or as a stream of individual vectors?
2026-09-05 11:34:55 [grok-build-0.1] 3. Is the vector display meant to be relatively small in the UI, or take up a significant portion
2026-09-05 11:34:55 [grok-build-0.1] of the window?
2026-09-05 11:34:55 [grok-build-0.1] 4. Do you care about frame-to-frame persistence, or should it be redrawn cleanly every update?
2026-09-05 11:34:55 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:34:55 [grok-build-0.1] This use case is quite different from normal 3D or UI work, so the usual Godot approaches often
2026-09-05 11:34:55 [grok-build-0.1] fight against the desired aesthetic.
