2026-09-05 11:36:05 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:36:05 [grok-build-0.1] Most Important Considerations Right Now
2026-09-05 11:36:05 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:36:05 [grok-build-0.1] • 1. 2D Canvas is the right domain*
2026-09-05 11:36:05 [grok-build-0.1] For pure vector lines (especially as a baseline), stay in 2D inside the SubViewport. Using 3D
2026-09-05 11:36:05 [grok-build-0.1] geometry or 3D line rendering adds unnecessary complexity and usually worse results for thin, clean
2026-09-05 11:36:05 [grok-build-0.1] lines. Treat the vector display as a 2D canvas problem, even if the rest of your project mixes
2026-09-05 11:36:05 [grok-build-0.1] 2D/3D.
2026-09-05 11:36:05 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:36:05 [grok-build-0.1] • 2. Line rendering method is the biggest quality lever*
2026-09-05 11:36:05 [grok-build-0.1] This is where most people lose cleanliness:
2026-09-05 11:36:05 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:36:05 [grok-build-0.1] - Standard `draw_line()` or default materials tend to look jagged or blurry when rendered to a
2026-09-05 11:36:05 [grok-build-0.1] texture.
