2026-09-05 11:37:29 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:37:29 [grok-build-0.1] For maximum simplicity, redrawing once per frame (even if you have partial data) is often cleaner
2026-09-05 11:37:29 [grok-build-0.1] than trying to react to every incoming packet.
2026-09-05 11:37:29 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:37:29 [grok-build-0.1] 7. Performance Reality Check
2026-09-05 11:37:29 [grok-build-0.1] Since lines are discardable, you have some freedom:
2026-09-05 11:37:29 [grok-build-0.1] - You can afford to throw away and recreate drawing elements every frame.
2026-09-05 11:37:29 [grok-build-0.1] - You don’t need to optimize for reuse or object pooling yet.
2026-09-05 11:37:29 [grok-build-0.1] - However, if the number of lines gets high, even a simple approach can start to feel heavy if
2026-09-05 11:37:29 [grok-build-0.1] you’re creating hundreds of `Line2D` nodes every frame.
2026-09-05 11:37:29 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:37:29 [grok-build-0.1] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-05 11:37:29 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:37:29 [grok-build-0.1] Bottom Line Recommendation (for keeping it simple)
2026-09-05 11:37:29 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:37:29 [grok-build-0.1] For a clean baseline, the strongest path is usually:
2026-09-05 11:37:29 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:37:29 [grok-build-0.1] - Render inside a `SubViewport` using 2D canvas drawing.
2026-09-05 11:37:29 [grok-build-0.1] - Accept a list of lines per frame from the simulator.
2026-09-05 11:37:29 [grok-build-0.1] - Clear and redraw everything fresh each frame.
2026-09-05 11:37:29 [grok-build-0.1] - Use either a very lightweight line shader or careful `draw_line()` calls rather than lots of
2026-09-05 11:37:29 [grok-build-0.1] `Line2D` nodes.
2026-09-05 11:37:29 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:37:29 [grok-build-0.1] This keeps the logic straightforward while giving you direct control over line quality.
2026-09-05 11:37:29 [grok-build-0.1] 
