2026-09-05 11:40:10 [grok-build-0.1] • Good, this is very useful context.*
2026-09-05 11:40:10 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:40:10 [grok-build-0.1] This is the classic Atari DVG (Digital Vector Generator) behavior. Here's how I see this affecting
2026-09-05 11:40:10 [grok-build-0.1] the Godot side, focusing on what matters for keeping things simple and clean.
2026-09-05 11:40:10 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:40:10 [grok-build-0.1] 1. Godot Should Not Interpret DVG Opcodes
2026-09-05 11:40:10 [grok-build-0.1] The most important architectural decision:
2026-09-05 11:40:10 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:40:10 [grok-build-0.1] - The emulator/simulator side (your TypeScript code) should do the hard work of executing
2026-09-05 11:40:10 [grok-build-0.1] the opcode stream (LABS, VCTR, SVEC, JSRL, RTSL, etc.).
2026-09-05 11:40:10 [grok-build-0.1] - Godot should receive a flat list of finished lines for each frame.
2026-09-05 11:40:10 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:40:10 [grok-build-0.1] Trying to run DVG opcodes on the Godot side would add unnecessary complexity (subroutine stacks,
2026-09-05 11:40:10 [grok-build-0.1] scale handling, bank switching, etc.). Keep the protocol dumb on the receiving end.
2026-09-05 11:40:10 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:40:10 [grok-build-0.1] 2. What a Frame Should Look Like to Godot
2026-09-05 11:40:10 [grok-build-0.1] For a clean baseline, the ideal payload per frame is something like:
2026-09-05 11:40:10 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:40:10 [grok-build-0.1] - A list of vectors
2026-09-05 11:40:10 [grok-build-0.1] - Each vector contains:
2026-09-05 11:40:10 [grok-build-0.1]   - Start position (x, y)
2026-09-05 11:40:10 [grok-build-0.1]   - End position (x, y)
2026-09-05 11:40:10 [grok-build-0.1]   - Brightness / intensity (0–15 or normalized 0.0–1.0)
2026-09-05 11:40:10 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:40:10 [grok-build-0.1] This matches how the DVG actually works after all the opcode processing is done. The JSRL/RTSL
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] subroutines should be flattened on the emulator side before sending.
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] 3. Double Buffering Behavior
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] The fact that the Atari side uses bank flipping (4000 / 4400) is actually helpful for us:
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] - One bank can be drawn by the DVG while the CPU prepares the next.
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] - On the Godot side, you can treat incoming frames as complete snapshots.
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] - You don’t need to worry about partial frames or mid-draw updates (assuming the simulator only
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] sends a frame when the DVG reaches HALT).
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] This fits very well with your “full redraw every frame, discardable” requirement.
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] 4. Timing and When to Send
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] Key points for the protocol:
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] - Only send a frame to Godot when the DVG has finished (i.e. after HALT).
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] - You probably don’t want to send every individual opcode or every small vector as it’s drawn. That
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] would create too much traffic and jitter.
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] - Sending one complete frame when the DVG finishes is much cleaner.
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] This also means Godot can simply replace the entire vector list each time it receives a new frame.
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] 5. Coordinate and Scale Considerations
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] From the DVG side you’ll need to decide:
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] - What coordinate range are you sending? (Classic DVG used roughly -1024 to +1023 or similar)
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] - Are you sending the raw DVG coordinates, or are you normalizing them (e.g. -1 to +1 or 0 to
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] viewport size)?
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] - Scale information from LABS — does the simulator resolve this before sending, or do you want
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] Godot to handle global scaling?
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] For a simple baseline, it’s usually cleaner if the emulator resolves position + scale and just
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] sends final screen-space (or normalized) line coordinates.
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] 6. Brightness
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] Brightness is important for the vector look. Even for a clean baseline, you should probably carry
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] brightness through so you can at least modulate line width or alpha later. Ignoring it completely
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] early on can make everything look flat.
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] Summary – Recommended Mental Model
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] ╭───────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────╮
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] │  Atari Side                   │  Godot Side                           │  Recommendation                           │
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] ├───────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────┤
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] │  Runs DVG opcodes             │  Receives processed lines             │  Emulator does the opcode work            │
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] │  Bank switching               │  Just receives complete frames        │  Send only on HALT                        │
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] │  JSRL / RTSL                  │  Should not exist on Godot side       │  Flatten on emulator side                 │
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] │  Per-frame redraw             │  Replace entire display each frame    │  Simple and matches your goal             │
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] │  Brightness                   │  Should be sent                       │  Useful even for baseline                 │
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] ╰───────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────╯
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
