2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] Questions that would help refine this:
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] 1. Do you want to send raw DVG-style coordinates and let Godot do the final scaling, or normalize
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] on the emulator side before sending?
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] 2. How often do you expect frames to be sent? (e.g. every time the DVG halts, or throttled to 60
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] fps?)
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] 3. Will brightness be sent as the original 0–15 value, or normalized?
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] This setup is actually quite friendly for a clean implementation on the Godot side, as long as the
2026-09-05 11:40:11 [grok-build-0.1] emulator side does the opcode interpretation and sends finished line lists.
