2026-09-05 11:43:12 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:43:12 [grok-build-0.1] How Clean Can 2D Vector Lines Be Represented in glTF?
2026-09-05 11:43:12 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:43:12 [grok-build-0.1] It can be reasonably clean if you treat glTF purely as a typed buffer container,
2026-09-05 11:43:12 [grok-build-0.1] not as a full 3D asset.
2026-09-05 11:43:12 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:43:12 [grok-build-0.1] Recommended Representation (Cleanest Path)
2026-09-05 11:43:13 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:43:13 [grok-build-0.1] Use a minimal `Mesh` with `mode: 1` (LINES):
2026-09-05 11:43:13 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:43:13 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:43:13 [grok-build-0.1] {
2026-09-05 11:43:13 [grok-build-0.1]   "meshes": [{
2026-09-05 11:43:13 [grok-build-0.1]     "primitives": [{
2026-09-05 11:43:13 [grok-build-0.1]       "mode": 1,
2026-09-05 11:43:13 [grok-build-0.1]       "attributes": {
2026-09-05 11:43:13 [grok-build-0.1]         "POSITION": 0,
2026-09-05 11:43:13 [grok-build-0.1]         "COLOR_0": 1     // optional: for brightness
2026-09-05 11:43:13 [grok-build-0.1]       }
2026-09-05 11:43:13 [grok-build-0.1]     }]
2026-09-05 11:43:13 [grok-build-0.1]   }]
2026-09-05 11:43:13 [grok-build-0.1] }
2026-09-05 11:43:13 [grok-build-0.1] 
