2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.2 grok-build-0.1 𝕏 🪠 0.7° $0.055 156.8KB 10.75s
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] • Here's the clean way to go from raw base64 to a `PackedVector2Array` in GDScript.*
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] Recommended Function
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] func base64_to_vec2_array(base64: String) -> PackedVector2Array:
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] 	var bytes: PackedByteArray = Marshalls.base64_to_raw(base64)
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] 	var result := PackedVector2Array()
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] 	# Assumes tightly packed float32 VEC2 (8 bytes per point)
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] 	for i in range(0, bytes.size(), 8):
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] 		var x := bytes.decode_float(i)
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] 		var y := bytes.decode_float(i + 4)
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] 		result.append(Vector2(x, y))
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] 	return result
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] Usage Example
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] # Example: you received this as part of your glTF buffer
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] var base64_buffer: String = "..."   # the base64 string from the message
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] var lines: PackedVector2Array = base64_to_vec2_array(base64_buffer)
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] # Now you can draw them
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] for i in range(0, lines.size(), 2):
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] 	var start := lines[i]
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] 	var end   := lines[i + 1]
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] 	draw_line(start, end, Color.WHITE, 1.0)
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] Important Notes for Your Case
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] - `decode_float()` reads little-endian float32, which matches glTF.
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] - This assumes tight packing (no stride/padding between points). This is the most common
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] case when generating minimal glTF for vector data.
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] - Each `Vector2` takes 8 bytes (2 × 4-byte floats).
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] - If your data has a stride (e.g. interleaved with other attributes), you’ll need to adjust the
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] step size.
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] Slightly More Robust Version
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] If you want to be a bit safer and handle the accessor’s `byteOffset` and `count`:
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] func base64_to_vec2_array(base64: String, byte_offset: int = 0, count: int = -1) -> PackedVector2Array:
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] 	var bytes: PackedByteArray = Marshalls.base64_to_raw(base64)
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] 	var result := PackedVector2Array()
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] 	var start := byte_offset
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] 	var end := bytes.size()
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:48:12 [grok-build-0.1] 	if count > 0:
2026-09-05 11:48:13 [grok-build-0.1] 		end = start + (count * 8)
2026-09-05 11:48:13 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:48:13 [grok-build-0.1] 	for i in range(start, end, 8):
2026-09-05 11:48:13 [grok-build-0.1] 		var x := bytes.decode_float(i)
2026-09-05 11:48:13 [grok-build-0.1] 		var y := bytes.decode_float(i + 4)
2026-09-05 11:48:13 [grok-build-0.1] 		result.append(Vector2(x, y))
2026-09-05 11:48:13 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:48:13 [grok-build-0.1] 	return result
2026-09-05 11:48:13 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:48:13 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 11:48:13 [grok-build-0.1] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
