2026-09-05 12:23:15 [grok-build-0.1] Current Behavior
2026-09-05 12:23:15 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:15 [grok-build-0.1] In your setup, the `log_view` is usually on top, but not because of the `@onready` keyword
2026-09-05 12:23:15 [grok-build-0.1] itself. It's because of child order and how Godot draws things.
2026-09-05 12:23:15 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:15 [grok-build-0.1] Here's what's actually happening:
2026-09-05 12:23:15 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:15 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:15 [grok-build-0.1] @onready var log_view = TextEdit.new()
2026-09-05 12:23:15 [grok-build-0.1] ...
2026-09-05 12:23:15 [grok-build-0.1] add_child(log_view)     # This runs in _ready()
2026-09-05 12:23:15 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:15 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:15 [grok-build-0.1] This adds the `TextEdit` as a child of the `Node` (the networking node).
2026-09-05 12:23:15 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:15 [grok-build-0.1] Your current scene hierarchy looks like this:
2026-09-05 12:23:15 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:15 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:15 [grok-build-0.1] Control
2026-09-05 12:23:15 [grok-build-0.1] ├── Node
2026-09-05 12:23:15 [grok-build-0.1] │   └── TextEdit (log_view)     ← Added here
2026-09-05 12:23:15 [grok-build-0.1] └── Node2D
2026-09-05 12:23:15 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:15 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:15 [grok-build-0.1] Why it usually appears on top:
2026-09-05 12:23:15 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:15 [grok-build-0.1] - Godot draws children in the order they appear in the scene tree.
2026-09-05 12:23:15 [grok-build-0.1] - Later siblings are drawn on top of earlier ones.
2026-09-05 12:23:15 [grok-build-0.1] - The `TextEdit` is a `Control`, and the `Node2D` is a `CanvasItem`. When mixed under a `Control`
2026-09-05 12:23:15 [grok-build-0.1] root, the UI element (`TextEdit`) tends to render after custom drawing from `Node2D`.
2026-09-05 12:23:15 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] So in practice, the log is currently covering your vector lines.
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] How to Control This
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] Here are your main options, from simplest to better:
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] 1. Quick & Dirty (Move the Node2D on top)
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] Add this in the `Node`'s `_ready()`, after adding the log view:
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] func _ready():
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1]     ...
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1]     add_child(log_view)
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1]     # Push the Node2D in front of the log
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1]     var node2d = get_node("../Node2D")
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1]     node2d.move_to_front()
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] 2. Better: Put the log view directly under Control (Recommended)
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] Instead of adding the `TextEdit` to the `Node`, add it to the `Control` root. This gives you more
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] control.
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] Change:
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] add_child(log_view)
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] To:
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] get_parent().add_child(log_view)
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] Then you can use `move_child()` to explicitly control order.
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] 3. Use Z-Index (More explicit)
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] On the `Node2D`, you can force it to draw above or below:
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] # In node2d.gd
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] z_index = 10          # Higher = drawn on top
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] Or on the log view:
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] log_view.z_index = 5
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] Quick Question:
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] Do you want the log view on top of the vector graphics (like a HUD), or do you want the
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] vector lines on top of the log?
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] Tell me which one you prefer and I’ll give you the cleanest way to set it up.
2026-09-05 12:23:16 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:34:07 [nitro@ryzen5] headless godot options
2026-09-05 13:34:26 [grok-build-0.1] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.2 grok-build-0.1 𝕏 🪠 0.7° $0.001 485B 17.27s
2026-09-05 13:34:26 [grok-build-0.1] • Godot Headless Options*
2026-09-05 13:34:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:34:26 [grok-build-0.1] Godot supports a proper headless mode using the `--headless` flag. This disables the window,
2026-09-05 13:34:26 [grok-build-0.1] rendering, and most graphics-related systems.
2026-09-05 13:34:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:34:26 [grok-build-0.1] Basic Headless Commands
2026-09-05 13:34:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:34:26 [grok-build-0.1] ╭──────────────────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
2026-09-05 13:34:26 [grok-build-0.1] │  Command                                     │  Description                                        │
2026-09-05 13:34:26 [grok-build-0.1] ├──────────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
2026-09-05 13:34:26 [grok-build-0.1] │  `godot --headless`                          │  Run Godot in headless mode (no window)             │
2026-09-05 13:34:26 [grok-build-0.1] │  `godot --headless --quit`                   │  Run headless and exit immediately (useful for CI)  │
2026-09-05 13:34:26 [grok-build-0.1] │  `godot --headless --path /path/to/project`  │  Run a specific project headless                    │
2026-09-05 13:34:26 [grok-build-0.1] ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
2026-09-05 13:34:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:34:26 [grok-build-0.1] Common Use Cases
2026-09-05 13:34:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:34:26 [grok-build-0.1] • 1. Run a script headless*
2026-09-05 13:34:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:34:26 [grok-build-0.1] godot --headless --script res://scripts/my_script.gd
2026-09-05 13:34:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:34:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] • 2. Export a project (recommended in CI)*
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] # Godot 4
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] godot --headless --export-release "Linux" ./build/game
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] # Godot 3
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] godot --headless --export "Linux/X11" ./build/game
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] • 3. Run a dedicated server*
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] godot --headless --main-pack game.pck
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] # or
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] godot --headless res://server/server.tscn
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] • 4. CI / Testing*
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] godot --headless --quit
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] # or with a test script
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] godot --headless --script res://tests/run_tests.gd --quit
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] Additional Useful Flags with Headless
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] ╭────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] │  Flag                      │  Purpose                                             │
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] ├────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] │  `--disable-render-loop`   │  Disables the render loop (can save some CPU)        │
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] │  `--audio-driver Dummy`    │  Use dummy audio driver                              │
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] │  `--display-driver dummy`  │  Use dummy display driver                            │
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] │  `--verbose`               │  More output (helpful when debugging headless runs)  │
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] │  `--no-header`             │  Cleaner output in CI                                │
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] │  `--fixed-fps 60`          │  Force a fixed frame rate                            │
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] ╰────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] Full Example (CI-style)
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] godot --headless \
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1]   --path /path/to/project \
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1]   --audio-driver Dummy \
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1]   --display-driver dummy \
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1]   --script res://ci/build_and_test.gd \
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1]   --quit
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] Notes
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] - `--headless` is the modern/recommended way (Godot 4+).
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] - In Godot 3, `--headless` also works, but some people used `--no-window` instead.
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] - For dedicated servers, consider building a Server export template instead of relying only
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] on `--headless` for better performance.
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] Would you like the options focused on a specific use case (CI, dedicated server, exporting, etc.)?
2026-09-05 13:34:27 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:48:11 [nitro@ryzen5] is there a dump docs or api -- flag?
2026-09-05 13:48:25 [grok-build-0.1] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.2 grok-build-0.1 𝕏 🪠 0.7° $0.002 3.775KB 13.33s
2026-09-05 13:48:25 [grok-build-0.1] Yes, Godot has several command-line flags for dumping documentation and API information. These work
2026-09-05 13:48:25 [grok-build-0.1] well with `--headless`.
2026-09-05 13:48:25 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:48:25 [grok-build-0.1] Here are the relevant flags:
2026-09-05 13:48:25 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:48:25 [grok-build-0.1] Main Documentation Flags
2026-09-05 13:48:25 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:48:25 [grok-build-0.1] ╭─────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────╮
2026-09-05 13:48:25 [grok-build-0.1] │  Flag                               │  Description                                                                  │  Typical Use Case                           │
2026-09-05 13:48:25 [grok-build-0.1] ├─────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────┤
2026-09-05 13:48:25 [grok-build-0.1] │  `--doctool`                        │  Generates or updates class reference documentation (XML)                     │  Updating docs or generating project docs   │
2026-09-05 13:48:25 [grok-build-0.1] │  `--dump-extension-api`             │  Dumps the full GDExtension API as `extension_api.json`                       │  GDExtension / C++ binding development      │
2026-09-05 13:48:25 [grok-build-0.1] │  `--dump-gdextension-interface`     │  Dumps the `gdextension_interface.h` header                                   │  GDExtension development                    │
2026-09-05 13:48:25 [grok-build-0.1] ╰─────────────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────╯
2026-09-05 13:48:25 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:48:25 [grok-build-0.1] Usage Examples
2026-09-05 13:48:25 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:48:25 [grok-build-0.1] • 1. Dump the GDExtension API (most commonly used)*
2026-09-05 13:48:25 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:48:25 [grok-build-0.1] godot --headless --dump-extension-api
2026-09-05 13:48:25 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:48:25 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:48:25 [grok-build-0.1] This will create a file called `extension_api.json` in the current directory.
2026-09-05 13:48:25 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:48:25 [grok-build-0.1] You can also specify an output path:
2026-09-05 13:48:25 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:48:25 [grok-build-0.1] godot --headless --dump-extension-api ./api/extension_api.json
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] • 2. Generate documentation with `--doctool`*
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] # Basic usage (dumps current engine classes)
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] godot --headless --doctool
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] # Point to a specific output folder
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] godot --headless --doctool ./docs
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] • 3. Generate documentation for your own project/classes*
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] godot --headless --doctool res:// --path /path/to/your/project
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] • 4. Dump the GDExtension interface header*
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] godot --headless --dump-gdextension-interface
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] Practical Examples
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] # Dump extension API (very common for GDExtension)
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] godot --headless --dump-extension-api extension_api.json
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] # Generate documentation in a specific folder
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] godot --headless --doctool ./class_reference
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] # Combine with project path
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] godot --headless --path /path/to/project --dump-extension-api
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] Notes
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] - `--dump-extension-api` is the one most people look for when working with GDExtension or external
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] tools.
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] - `--doctool` is mainly used when contributing to Godot itself or when you want to generate XML
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] documentation for your own classes.
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] - These flags generally work in both Godot 3 and Godot 4, though `--dump-extension-api` is more
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] relevant in Godot 4+.
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] Would you like me to show how to use these for a specific purpose (e.g. GDExtension development,
2026-09-05 13:48:26 [grok-build-0.1] generating docs for your project, etc.)?
