2026-09-05 13:52:52 [nitro@ryzen5] is godot upto supporting publishing serious games to steam?
2026-09-05 13:53:08 [grok-build-0.1] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.2 grok-build-0.1 𝕏 🪠 0.7° $0.002 3.904KB 15.33s
2026-09-05 13:53:08 [grok-build-0.1] Yes, Godot can be used to publish serious games on Steam, and people are already doing it
2026-09-05 13:53:08 [grok-build-0.1] successfully. However, whether it's a good choice depends on the scale and type of game
2026-09-05 13:53:08 [grok-build-0.1] you're making.
2026-09-05 13:53:08 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:53:08 [grok-build-0.1] Here's a realistic breakdown:
2026-09-05 13:53:08 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:53:08 [grok-build-0.1] Current State (Godot 4.x)
2026-09-05 13:53:08 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:53:08 [grok-build-0.1] ╭────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────╮
2026-09-05 13:53:08 [grok-build-0.1] │  Aspect                            │  Status                                       │  Notes                                        │
2026-09-05 13:53:08 [grok-build-0.1] ├────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────┤
2026-09-05 13:53:08 [grok-build-0.1] │  **Publishing to Steam**           │  Good                                         │  Many games have shipped successfully         │
2026-09-05 13:53:08 [grok-build-0.1] │  **Steamworks Integration**        │  Decent                                       │  Official GDExtension exists                  │
2026-09-05 13:53:08 [grok-build-0.1] │  **2D Games**                      │  Very strong                                  │  Excellent for serious 2D games               │
2026-09-05 13:53:08 [grok-build-0.1] │  **3D Games**                      │  Acceptable but more work                     │  Improving, but still behind Unreal           │
2026-09-05 13:53:08 [grok-build-0.1] │  **Large scope / Big teams**       │  Possible but harder                          │  Tooling and performance require more effort  │
2026-09-05 13:53:08 [grok-build-0.1] │  **Performance optimization**      │  Improving                                    │  Better in 4.3+, but not automatic            │
2026-09-05 13:53:08 [grok-build-0.1] │  **Stability for commercial use**  │  Good (4.3+)                                  │  Much better than Godot 3                     │
2026-09-05 13:53:08 [grok-build-0.1] ╰────────────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────────╯
2026-09-05 13:53:08 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:53:08 [grok-build-0.1] Real-World Examples
2026-09-05 13:53:08 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:53:08 [grok-build-0.1] Godot has been used for several commercially successful Steam releases, including:
2026-09-05 13:53:08 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:53:08 [grok-build-0.1] - Cassette Beasts (highly rated RPG)
2026-09-05 13:53:08 [grok-build-0.1] - Dome Keeper
2026-09-05 13:53:08 [grok-build-0.1] - Brotato
2026-09-05 13:53:08 [grok-build-0.1] - The Cosmic Wheel Sisterhood
2026-09-05 13:53:08 [grok-build-0.1] - The Last Spell
2026-09-05 13:53:08 [grok-build-0.1] - Tails Noir
2026-09-05 13:53:08 [grok-build-0.1] - Godot Wild Jam winners and various mid-sized indie titles
2026-09-05 13:53:08 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:53:08 [grok-build-0.1] These are mostly mid-sized indie games rather than big-budget AA or AAA titles.
2026-09-05 13:53:08 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:53:08 [grok-build-0.1] Important Limitations
2026-09-05 13:53:08 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:53:08 [grok-build-0.1] Here are the main things to consider if you're aiming for a "serious" game:
2026-09-05 13:53:08 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:53:09 [grok-build-0.1] - 3D is still the weakest area: If you're making a large, complex 3D game (especially with
2026-09-05 13:53:09 [grok-build-0.1] heavy graphics or open worlds), Unreal Engine is generally more mature and less painful.
2026-09-05 13:53:09 [grok-build-0.1] - Team size & tooling: Godot lacks some of the advanced collaboration and large-project
2026-09-05 13:53:09 [grok-build-0.1] tools that Unity and Unreal have.
2026-09-05 13:53:09 [grok-build-0.1] - Performance: You often need to do more manual optimization, especially in 3D or with
2026-09-05 13:53:09 [grok-build-0.1] complex gameplay systems.
2026-09-05 13:53:09 [grok-build-0.1] - Steamworks: The integration works, but it's not as seamless as Unity's or Unreal's
2026-09-05 13:53:09 [grok-build-0.1] built-in plugins. You'll be using a GDExtension.
2026-09-05 13:53:09 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-05 13:53:09 [grok-build-0.1] Recommendation
2026-09-05 13:53:09 [grok-build-0.1] 
