2026-09-07 08:30:45 [gemini-3.8-flash] 3. Indefinite Blocking in `snoopComplete()`
2026-09-07 08:30:45 [gemini-3.8-flash] `snoopComplete()` monitors `!dma_channel_is_busy()`. The DMA channel will only finish when all
2026-09-07 08:30:45 [gemini-3.8-flash] 8,192 words (4,096 transitions) have been pushed by the PIO.
2026-09-07 08:30:45 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-07 08:30:45 [gemini-3.8-flash] If the 6502 halts, enters a tight loop without address changes, or the bus goes idle,
2026-09-07 08:30:45 [gemini-3.8-flash] `snoopComplete()` will never return, locking the main loop in:
2026-09-07 08:30:45 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-07 08:30:45 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-07 08:30:45 [gemini-3.8-flash] while (!snoopComplete()) {
2026-09-07 08:30:45 [gemini-3.8-flash] 	watchdog_update();
2026-09-07 08:30:45 [gemini-3.8-flash] 	tud_task();
2026-09-07 08:30:45 [gemini-3.8-flash] 	sleep_ms(1);
2026-09-07 08:30:45 [gemini-3.8-flash] }
2026-09-07 08:30:45 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-07 08:30:45 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-07 08:30:45 [gemini-3.8-flash] Adding an elapsed timeout or checking for an abort condition ensures control returns to the shell
2026-09-07 08:30:45 [gemini-3.8-flash] even if the bus goes quiet before `MAX_SAMPLES` is reached.
