2026-09-07 08:38:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] Here are a few observations on the updated `snoop.cpp`:
2026-09-07 08:38:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-07 08:38:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 1. FIFO Flush and State Machine Synchronization
2026-09-07 08:38:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] Because `pio_sm_set_enabled(snoop_pio, snoop_sm, true)` is invoked in `initSnoop()`, the state
2026-09-07 08:38:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] machine runs continuously in the background. Prior to calling `beginSnoop()`, any bus transitions
2026-09-07 08:38:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] push words into the RX FIFO.
2026-09-07 08:38:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-07 08:38:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] To ensure the DMA begins reading on an aligned pair boundary (tick first, pins second) rather than
2026-09-07 08:38:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] picking up stale words:
2026-09-07 08:38:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Disabling the state machine or draining the FIFO via `pio_sm_clear_fifos(snoop_pio, snoop_sm)`
2026-09-07 08:38:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] right before starting the transfer ensures the FIFO is clean.
2026-09-07 08:38:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Restarting or clearing execution state with `pio_sm_restart(snoop_pio, snoop_sm)` and
2026-09-07 08:38:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] `pio_sm_clkdiv_restart(snoop_pio, snoop_sm)` guarantees the PIO routine begins at a known state.
2026-09-07 08:38:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-07 08:38:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 2. Remaining Transfer Truncation in `getCapturedSampleCount`
2026-09-07 08:38:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] In `getCapturedSampleCount()`:
2026-09-07 08:38:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-07 08:38:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] return snoopRequested-(dma_channel_hw_addr(snoop_dma_chan)->transfer_count/2);
2026-09-07 08:38:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-07 08:38:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] When `stopBusCapture()` is called mid-transfer and an odd number of 32-bit words has arrived, the
2026-09-07 08:38:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] integer division rounds in a way that includes the lone half-sample. Computing the completed pairs
2026-09-07 08:38:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] from the words transferred avoids reading past valid pairs:
2026-09-07 08:38:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-07 08:38:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] size_t totalWords = snoopRequested * 2;
