2026-09-07 10:07:04 [gemini-3.8-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.2 gemini-3.8-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.006 25.36KB 4.47s
2026-09-07 10:07:04 [gemini-3.8-flash] In USB CDC-ACM (and TinyUSB's implementation on the RP2040), RTS stands for Request To
2026-09-07 10:07:04 [gemini-3.8-flash] Send.
2026-09-07 10:07:04 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-07 10:07:04 [gemini-3.8-flash] In the context of `cdcStatus()`:
2026-09-07 10:07:04 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-07 10:07:04 [gemini-3.8-flash] 1. Virtual Control Line:
2026-09-07 10:07:04 [gemini-3.8-flash]    Because native USB does not have physical RS-232 pins, the host driver communicates modern UART
2026-09-07 10:07:04 [gemini-3.8-flash] flow-control signals via CDC control packets (`SET_CONTROL_LINE_STATE`). RTS is transmitted as bit
2026-09-07 10:07:04 [gemini-3.8-flash] 1 of the control line bitmap (bit 0 is DTR, Data Terminal Ready).
2026-09-07 10:07:04 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-07 10:07:04 [gemini-3.8-flash] 2. Terminal / Host Connection State:
2026-09-07 10:07:04 [gemini-3.8-flash]    When a terminal emulator (such as PuTTY, minicom, or a WebUSB serial console) opens the virtual
2026-09-07 10:07:04 [gemini-3.8-flash] COM port, it typically asserts DTR and RTS together:
2026-09-07 10:07:04 [gemini-3.8-flash]    * DTR (bit 0, value `0x01`): Host terminal indicates it is present and connected.
2026-09-07 10:07:04 [gemini-3.8-flash]    * RTS (bit 1, value `0x02`): Host terminal signals it is ready to receive incoming bulk
2026-09-07 10:07:04 [gemini-3.8-flash] data from the device.
2026-09-07 10:07:04 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-07 10:07:04 [gemini-3.8-flash] 3. Status Mask (`status & 3`):
2026-09-07 10:07:04 [gemini-3.8-flash]    In your code:
2026-09-07 10:07:04 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-07 10:07:04 [gemini-3.8-flash]    int status = cdcStatus();
2026-09-07 10:07:04 [gemini-3.8-flash]    if (status & 3) { ... }
2026-09-07 10:07:04 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-07 10:07:04 [gemini-3.8-flash]    * A mask of `3` checks both `DTR | RTS` (`0x01 | 0x02`).
2026-09-07 10:07:04 [gemini-3.8-flash]    * When `status & 3` evaluates to non-zero, it usually means the USB host has opened the COM port
2026-09-07 10:07:04 [gemini-3.8-flash] and signaled that the device is free to stream trace packets over bulk endpoints. When it drops to
2026-09-07 10:07:05 [gemini-3.8-flash] `0`, the host serial monitor has closed or disconnected.
2026-09-07 10:07:05 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
