2026-09-10 09:29:12 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-09-10 09:29:12 [claude-haiku-4-5] godotSchema.json.txt
2026-09-10 09:29:12 [claude-haiku-4-5] This is a comprehensive schema snapshot of Godot 4.7.2 with four main class categories:
2026-09-10 09:29:12 [claude-haiku-4-5] - editor: 58 editor-specific classes
2026-09-10 09:29:12 [claude-haiku-4-5] - node: 380+ Node-derived classes
2026-09-10 09:29:12 [claude-haiku-4-5] - object: 1000+ Object-derived classes
2026-09-10 09:29:12 [claude-haiku-4-5] - resource: 500+ Resource-derived classes
2026-09-10 09:29:12 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-09-10 09:29:12 [claude-haiku-4-5] Plus variant types and globals. Well-structured metadata document.
2026-09-10 09:29:12 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-09-10 09:29:12 [claude-haiku-4-5] scrapegodot.txt
2026-09-10 09:29:12 [claude-haiku-4-5] The GDScript scraper dynamically generates this schema from runtime ClassDB. Key observations:
2026-09-10 09:29:12 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-09-10 09:29:12 [claude-haiku-4-5] Strengths
2026-09-10 09:29:12 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Correctly categorizes classes by parent type (Node, Resource, Object)
2026-09-10 09:29:12 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Editor class detection via prefix matching (`Editor`, `ResourceImporter`)
2026-09-10 09:29:12 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Generates proper method signatures with types and defaults
2026-09-10 09:29:13 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Handles variant type enumeration
2026-09-10 09:29:13 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Outputs valid JSON
2026-09-10 09:29:13 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-09-10 09:29:13 [claude-haiku-4-5] Potential Issues
2026-09-10 09:29:13 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-09-10 09:29:13 [claude-haiku-4-5] 1. Category Overlap: The populate_categories function adds classes to multiple lists if
2026-09-10 09:29:13 [claude-haiku-4-5] they inherit from multiple types. For example, `EditorScript` inherits from both `Script`
2026-09-10 09:29:13 [claude-haiku-4-5] (Resource) and potentially gets added to both categories. The schema JSON shows some classes
2026-09-10 09:29:13 [claude-haiku-4-5] appearing in multiple sections.
2026-09-10 09:29:13 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-09-10 09:29:13 [claude-haiku-4-5] 2. Missing Globals: The scraper hardcodes `@GDScript` and `@GlobalScope` but doesn't
2026-09-10 09:29:13 [claude-haiku-4-5] dynamically discover global functions. The schema file doesn't list individual global functions
2026-09-10 09:29:13 [claude-haiku-4-5] either.
2026-09-10 09:29:13 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-09-10 09:29:13 [claude-haiku-4-5] 3. Type Resolution: The `getTypeName()` function handles built-in and class types, but the
2026-09-10 09:29:13 [claude-haiku-4-5] current schema doesn't include method/property definitions—only class categorization.
2026-09-10 09:29:13 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-09-10 09:29:13 [claude-haiku-4-5] 4. Editor Detection: Prefix-based detection is reasonable but fragile. Classes like
2026-09-10 09:29:13 [claude-haiku-4-5] `GDScriptEditorTranslationParserPlugin` would be correctly identified, but custom plugins might
2026-09-10 09:29:13 [claude-haiku-4-5] miss.
2026-09-10 09:29:13 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
