2026-09-11 14:10:29 [deepseek-flash] Here's what the three files are and how they relate.
2026-09-11 14:10:29 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:10:29 [deepseek-flash] What each file is
2026-09-11 14:10:29 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:10:29 [deepseek-flash] • 1. `scrapeschema.gd` (base64 payload)*
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] Decodes to a GDScript that `extends SceneTree`. Entry point is `_init()`, which calls
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] `scrapeSchema("res://godot_api_schema.json")` and then `quit()` — the "run once headless" shape. It
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] contains only the schema-building core: `get_variant_names`, `is_editor_class`,
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] `populate_categories`, `build_schema_dictionary`, `scrapeSchema`, plus a placeholder triple-quoted
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] docstring.
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] • 2. `scrapegodot.txt`*
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] Same core as (1), but `extends Node` and is driven from `_ready()` (with a no-op `_process`). It
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] adds five functions that are not present in (1): `formatParam`, `formatParamList`,
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] `getSignature`, `getTypeName`, `getSignatures`. These build human-readable method signatures from
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] `ClassDB.get_method_list`. Nothing in `build_schema_dictionary` calls them, so they're currently
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] dead code in this file.
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] • 3. `godotSchema.json.txt`*
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] The generated artifact. Its key set matches what both scripts emit, and the keys are alphabetically
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] ordered because `JSON.stringify` sorts keys by default. It contains no signature data, so it
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] corresponds to the shared schema shape — the extra helpers in (2) do not appear in it.
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] What is new / different
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] - Entry point / base class: `SceneTree` + `_init` + `quit` (file 1) vs `Node` + `_ready` +
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] `_process` (file 2).
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] - Superset: file 2 is file 1 plus the signature-formatting helpers, minus the docstring and
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] minus the `SceneTree` bootstrap. Everything else (`populate_categories`, category predicates,
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] `build_schema_dictionary`, `scrapeSchema`) is identical.
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] - `get_variant_names` is the same in both, and its output matches the JSON `variant` array
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] exactly — `"Variant"` is inserted first, then the rest are sorted, which is why `Variant` lands
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] between `Transform3D` and `Vector2`.
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] - `latest: "4.7.2"` in the JSON is just whatever `Engine.get_version_info()` returned at
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] generation time; the schema's own `version` is `"0.1.0"`.
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] Consistency checks I ran
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] - The `node`, `resource`, `object`, and `editor` arrays in the JSON are all consistent with
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] `ClassDB.is_parent_class(current_name, "<ancestor>")` as written (walking up from
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] `current_name`), so the `object` array being the full class list is expected, not a bug.
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] - `editor` matches `is_editor_class` — the `Editor` and `ResourceImporter` prefix filter.
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] Minor things worth noting
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] - Naming drift: the scripts write to `res://godot_api_schema.json`, but the shared artifact
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] is named `godotSchema.json.txt`. Looks like an export/rename step rather than a code difference.
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] - Indentation: `scrapegodot.txt` mixes tabs and double-indented blocks (e.g. inside
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] `getSignature` and `get_variant_names`). It's still valid GDScript, but it diverges from the
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] tab-consistent style in `scrapeschema.gd`.
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] - Unused capability: the signature helpers in `scrapegodot.txt` would let you enrich the
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] schema with method signatures, but they aren't wired into `build_schema_dictionary` yet, so no
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] schema output currently depends on them.
2026-09-11 14:10:30 [deepseek-flash] 
