2026-09-11 14:18:34 [deepseek-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.3 deepseek-flash 🐋 🪠 0.7° $0.002 3.272KB 7.99s
2026-09-11 14:18:34 [deepseek-flash] This is the standard Godot extension API entry for `VisualShaderNodeTransformParameter`. I don’t
2026-09-11 14:18:34 [deepseek-flash] have a previous dump to diff against, so I can’t say whether it’s newly added or changed, but the
2026-09-11 14:18:34 [deepseek-flash] shape looks consistent with Godot 4.x core API metadata.
2026-09-11 14:18:34 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:18:34 [deepseek-flash] A few observations:
2026-09-11 14:18:34 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:18:34 [deepseek-flash] - It is a refcounted, instantiable core class that inherits from `VisualShaderNodeParameter`.
2026-09-11 14:18:34 [deepseek-flash] - It exposes a boolean toggle and a `Transform3D` default value:
2026-09-11 14:18:35 [deepseek-flash]   - `default_value_enabled` uses `set_default_value_enabled()` / `is_default_value_enabled()`.
2026-09-11 14:18:35 [deepseek-flash]   - `default_value` uses `set_default_value()` / `get_default_value()`.
2026-09-11 14:18:35 [deepseek-flash] - The description says it translates to `uniform mat4` in the shader language. That matches Godot’s
2026-09-11 14:18:35 [deepseek-flash] mapping of `Transform3D` to a 4×4 matrix for shader uniforms.
2026-09-11 14:18:35 [deepseek-flash] - The `hash` values are method-signature hashes. They are engine-build-specific, so they are useful
2026-09-11 14:18:35 [deepseek-flash] for validation but not something to hardcode for cross-version compatibility.
2026-09-11 14:18:35 [deepseek-flash] - The naming is normal for Godot: boolean properties often use an `is_` getter rather than `get_`.
2026-09-11 14:18:35 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:18:35 [deepseek-flash] If you are comparing against an older `extension_api.json`, the main things to check would be
2026-09-11 14:18:35 [deepseek-flash] whether `default_value` and `default_value_enabled` were present before, and whether the hashes or
2026-09-11 14:18:35 [deepseek-flash] inheritance chain changed. If you share the previous file or a diff, I can point out the actual
2026-09-11 14:18:35 [deepseek-flash] additions or differences.
2026-09-11 14:18:35 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:26 [nitro@ryzen5] can you give me background intro to how the shader stack is comprised
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.3 deepseek-flash 🐋 🪠 0.7° $0.003 4.903KB 14.82s
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] Godot’s “shader stack” is easiest to understand as a set of layers that translate a high-level
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] description of appearance into GPU programs and state. The layers are roughly:
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] 1. Authoring layer — VisualShader graphs
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] 2. Shader resource layer — Shader and VisualShader
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] 3. Shader language layer — Godot Shading Language, shader types, and stages
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] 4. Parameter/uniform layer — global, material, instance, and built-in uniforms
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] 5. Compilation and backend layer — ShaderCompiler, RenderingDevice, and graphics APIs
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] 6. Rendering pipeline layer — renderers, passes, and draw/compute submission
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] 1. Authoring layer: VisualShader graphs
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] A `VisualShader` is a graph resource. Nodes represent operations, inputs, outputs, and parameters.
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] Connections define data flow.
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] Node categories include:
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] - Input nodes: vertex position, UV, normal, time, etc.
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] - Output nodes: fragment color, vertex position, etc.
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] - Math and vector nodes
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] - Texture nodes
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] - Transform nodes
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] - Parameter nodes
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] `VisualShaderNodeTransformParameter` is a parameter node. It defines a named `Transform3D` uniform
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] that can be set per material or per instance. In the generated shader it becomes a `mat4` uniform.
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] The `default_value_enabled` and `default_value` properties control whether a default transform is
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] baked into the shader or exposed as a uniform.
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] The graph is not sent to the GPU directly. It is compiled into shader code or an internal shader
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] representation.
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] 2. Shader resource layer: Shader and VisualShader
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] Both text-based `Shader` resources and `VisualShader` resources ultimately produce a `Shader`
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] object used by the rendering server.
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] A shader has:
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] - A shader type, such as `spatial`, `canvas_item`, `particles`, `sky`, `fog`, or `compute`
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] - One or more stages, depending on the type
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] - Render modes that affect pipeline state
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] - Uniforms, varyings, and built-in variables
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] The shader type determines which stages and built-ins are available. For example, a `spatial`
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] shader can have `vertex`, `fragment`, and `light` stages, while a `canvas_item` shader has `vertex`
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] and `fragment` stages.
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] 3. Shader language layer: Godot Shading Language
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:42 [deepseek-flash] Godot uses its own shader language, often called GDShader. It is similar to GLSL but with
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] Godot-specific syntax and built-ins.
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] Key parts:
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] - `shader_type` declares the shader type.
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] - `render_mode` changes rendering behavior.
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] - `uniform` declares externally settable values.
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] - `varying` passes data between stages.
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] - Built-ins like `VERTEX`, `FRAGCOORD`, `MODEL_MATRIX`, `TIME`, etc., are provided per stage.
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] Each stage has its own set of built-ins. The compiler validates that a shader only uses built-ins
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] valid for its type and stage.
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] 4. Parameter and uniform layer
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] Uniforms are the bridge between the scene/material and the shader. Godot has several levels:
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] - Global shader uniforms: project-wide values, often used for wind, time of day, etc.
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] - Material uniforms: set on a `ShaderMaterial` or `VisualShader` instance.
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] - Instance uniforms: per-instance values, useful for large numbers of objects.
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] - Built-in engine uniforms: camera matrices, time, screen texture, etc.
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] A `VisualShaderNodeTransformParameter` becomes a material-level uniform of type `mat4`. If you
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] enable instance uniforms, it can also be set per instance. The default value is used when no
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] override is provided.
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] 5. Compilation and backend layer
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] The `ShaderCompiler` parses and validates the shader, then generates backend-specific code:
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] - Vulkan: SPIR-V
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] - Direct3D 12: DXIL
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] - Metal: MSL
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] - OpenGL: GLSL
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] The `RenderingDevice` abstraction wraps these APIs. It manages shader modules, pipelines,
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] descriptor sets, and uniform buffers. Shader variants and specialization constants are used to
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] avoid recompiling the same shader for every minor difference.
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] 6. Rendering pipeline layer
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] At runtime, the renderer decides which shaders to use for each pass. Godot 4 has multiple
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] renderers:
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] - Forward+
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] - Mobile
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] - Compatibility
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] Each renderer has its own pipeline organization, but the general pass order includes:
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] - Shadow passes
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] - Depth prepass
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] - Opaque geometry
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] - Transparent geometry
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] - Post-processing
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] Shaders are bound to pipelines, uniforms are uploaded, and draw or compute commands are submitted
2026-09-11 14:19:43 [deepseek-flash] to the GPU.
2026-09-11 14:19:44 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:44 [deepseek-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-11 14:19:44 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:44 [deepseek-flash] Where `VisualShaderNodeTransformParameter` fits
2026-09-11 14:19:44 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:44 [deepseek-flash] It sits in the authoring layer as a parameter node. When the visual shader is compiled, it becomes
2026-09-11 14:19:44 [deepseek-flash] a `mat4` uniform in the generated shader. At runtime, that uniform is filled from the material’s
2026-09-11 14:19:44 [deepseek-flash] default value, a material override, or an instance override. The rendering backend then uploads it
2026-09-11 14:19:44 [deepseek-flash] to the GPU as part of the uniform buffer or push constant block.
2026-09-11 14:19:44 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:19:44 [deepseek-flash] If by “shader stack” you meant a specific part of this—such as the visual shader node evaluation
2026-09-11 14:19:44 [deepseek-flash] stack, the uniform binding stack, or the render pass stack—I can go deeper into that layer.
2026-09-11 14:19:44 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:57:50 [deepseek-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.3 deepseek-flash 🐋 🪠 0.7° $0.028 23.17KB 82.39s
2026-09-11 14:57:50 [deepseek-flash] These files are new relative to the earlier `extension_api.json` and the shader‑stack discussion.
2026-09-11 14:57:50 [deepseek-flash] That earlier material was about Godot’s shader authoring/compilation layers and a
2026-09-11 14:57:50 [deepseek-flash] `VisualShaderNodeTransformParameter` API entry. These four scripts are a runtime Godot 4 project
2026-09-11 14:57:50 [deepseek-flash] instead: a small networked drawing/logging app with a Godot class‑schema exporter.
2026-09-11 14:57:50 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:57:50 [deepseek-flash] What the scripts do
2026-09-11 14:57:50 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:57:50 [deepseek-flash] - `control.gd`
2026-09-11 14:57:50 [deepseek-flash]   A minimal `Control` node. It prints a banner in `_ready()` and does nothing in `_process()`.
2026-09-11 14:57:50 [deepseek-flash] Likely a placeholder or UI host.
2026-09-11 14:57:50 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:57:50 [deepseek-flash] - `node.gd`
2026-09-11 14:57:50 [deepseek-flash]   The main coordinator. It:
2026-09-11 14:57:50 [deepseek-flash]   - Creates a `TextEdit` for on‑screen diagnostics.
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash]   - Listens for WebSocket clients on TCP port `8080`.
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash]   - Connects upstream as a WebSocket client to `ws://localhost:9000`.
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash]   - Polls both the upstream socket and local clients each frame.
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash]   - Parses JSON messages and dispatches on `method`:
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash]     - `"snoop"` – asks the `Snoop` singleton for its schema and logs the JSON length.
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash]     - `"init"` – sends a hard‑coded splash‑screen line set to `$Node2D`.
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash]     - `"draw"` – decodes a base64 buffer into `PackedVector2Array` and sends it to `$Node2D`.
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash]     - `"tick"` – logs the message.
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash]   - Logs a frame counter and accumulated delta every 1024 frames.
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash] - `node2d.gd`
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash]   A `Node2D` that stores a `PackedVector2Array` of line endpoints and draws them in `_draw()` using
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash] `draw_line()`. `set_lines()` replaces the array and calls `queue_redraw()`.
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash] - `snoop.gd`
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash]   Intended to be an autoload singleton named `Snoop`. It builds a dictionary of Godot classes and
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash] their method names using `ClassDB`. It populates category arrays for `Node`, `Resource`, and
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash] `Object` subclasses, but only the `schema` dictionary is actually included in the returned result.
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash] Many fields are commented out. It also defines `getNodeSignatures()` but does not call it.
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash] Overall architecture
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash] The app acts as a relay/visualizer:
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash] - Upstream server (`:9000`) sends commands.
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash] - Local WebSocket clients (`:8080`) can also send commands.
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash] - Commands can trigger drawing on a `Node2D` or request a Godot API schema dump.
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash] - Diagnostics are shown in a `TextEdit` overlay.
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash] This is consistent with a tool like a Godot API explorer or remote‑controlled drawing surface. The
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash] repository URL in `snoop.gd` points to `github.com/nitrologic/biblispec`, so these scripts are
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash] probably part of that project.
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash] Potential issues
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash] 1. `params.buffer` can fail
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash]    In `node.gd`, `onPacket()` does:
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash]    var params = request.get("params", {})
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash]    ...
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash]    "draw":
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash]        var vec_lines = base64_to_vec2_array(params.buffer)
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash]    If the incoming JSON has no `params` or no `buffer` key, this will error. A safer form is
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash] `params.get("buffer", "")` with a guard.
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash] 2. `message.buffer` is invalid
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash]    The same `"draw"` branch logs:
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash]    glog("onPacket draw: " + message.buffer)
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash]    `message` is a `String`; it has no `.buffer` property. This should probably be `params.buffer`
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash] or just omit the buffer from the log.
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash] 3. `Snoop` singleton assumption
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash]    `node.gd` uses `var snoop = Snoop`. For this to work, `snoop.gd` must be registered as an
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash] autoload named `Snoop`. If it is not, `Snoop` will be an unresolved identifier. The script itself
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash] does not declare `class_name Snoop`.
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash] 4. Unused schema data
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash]    `snoopGodot()` extracts `args`, `rtype`, and `flags` for each method but never uses them. The
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash] `schema` only stores method names. If the goal is a full API description, those fields should be
2026-09-11 14:57:51 [deepseek-flash] included.
2026-09-11 14:57:52 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:57:52 [deepseek-flash] 5. No reconnect for upstream
2026-09-11 14:57:52 [deepseek-flash]    If the upstream WebSocket disconnects, `is_connected_upstream` is set to `false` but no
2026-09-11 14:57:52 [deepseek-flash] reconnection is attempted. Depending on requirements, a retry loop might be needed.
2026-09-11 14:57:52 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:57:52 [deepseek-flash] 6. `getNodeSignatures()` is dead code
2026-09-11 14:57:52 [deepseek-flash]    It is defined but never called. It also sorts an array of method dictionaries, which may not
2026-09-11 14:57:52 [deepseek-flash] sort meaningfully.
2026-09-11 14:57:52 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:57:52 [deepseek-flash] 7. `_process` in `node.gd` calls `pollNetwork()` every frame
2026-09-11 14:57:52 [deepseek-flash]    That is correct for WebSocket polling, but it also logs every 1024 frames. Fine for diagnostics,
2026-09-11 14:57:52 [deepseek-flash] though it adds a small overhead.
2026-09-11 14:57:52 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:57:52 [deepseek-flash] 8. `node2d.gd` uses `Color.WHITE` and width `1.0`
2026-09-11 14:57:52 [deepseek-flash]    This is fine, but if the line data is very large, `_draw()` will issue many `draw_line()` calls.
2026-09-11 14:57:52 [deepseek-flash] For large buffers, a single `draw_multiline()` would be more efficient.
2026-09-11 14:57:52 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 14:57:52 [deepseek-flash] Differences from previous content
