2026-09-11 15:05:15 [nitro@ryzen5] i want to send mime64 buffers in message and then send them out of band like glb
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.3 deepseek-flash 🐋 🪠 0.7° $0.004 41.05KB 12.22s
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] Good idea — WebSocket already has binary frames, so you don't need base64 at all for the payload.
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] You can mirror GLB’s chunked layout so one binary frame carries a JSON header plus a raw BIN chunk.
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] Frame layout (little-endian, GLB-style)
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] offset  size  field
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] 0       4     magic        'NTRL'
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] 4       4     version      1
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] 8       4     total length (whole frame)
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] 12      4     chunkLength  (JSON chunk, padded)
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] 16      4     chunkType    'JSON'
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] 20      n     JSON bytes, padded to 4 with 0x20
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] ...     4     chunkLength  (BIN chunk, padded)
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] ...     4     chunkType    'BIN\0'
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] ...     n     BIN bytes, padded to 4 with 0x00
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] `chunkLength` includes its own padding, matching glTF 2.0. Unknown chunk types are skipped.
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] Helpers
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] const FRAME_MAGIC := 0x4C52544E        # 'NTRL'
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] const FRAME_VERSION := 1
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] const CHUNK_JSON := 0x4E4F534A         # 'JSON'
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] const CHUNK_BIN  := 0x004E4942         # 'BIN\0'
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] func _pad4(n: int) -> int:
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] 	return (n + 3) & ~3
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] func build_frame(header: Dictionary, binary: PackedByteArray) -> PackedByteArray:
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] 	var json := JSON.stringify(header).to_utf8_buffer()
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] 	var json_len := _pad4(json.size())
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] 	var bin_len := _pad4(binary.size())
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] 	var out := PackedByteArray()
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] 	out.resize(12 + 8 + json_len + 8 + bin_len)
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] 	out.encode_u32(0, FRAME_MAGIC)
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] 	out.encode_u32(4, FRAME_VERSION)
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] 	out.encode_u32(8, out.size())
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] 	out.encode_u32(12, json_len)
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] 	out.encode_u32(16, CHUNK_JSON)
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] 	out.fill(0x20)                          # pad JSON with spaces
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] 	out.encode_u32(20 + json_len, bin_len)
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] 	out.encode_u32(24 + json_len, CHUNK_BIN)
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] 	out.fill(0x00)                          # pad BIN with zeros
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] 	out.encode_u32(8, out.size())           # rewrite after resize
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] 	return out
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] func parse_frame(data: PackedByteArray) -> Dictionary:
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] 	if data.size() < 12 or data.decode_u32(0) != FRAME_MAGIC:
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] 		return {}
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] 	var header := {}
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] 	var binary := PackedByteArray()
2026-09-11 15:05:28 [deepseek-flash] 	var off := 12
2026-09-11 15:05:29 [deepseek-flash] 	while off + 8 <= data.size():
2026-09-11 15:05:29 [deepseek-flash] 		var clen := data.decode_u32(off)
2026-09-11 15:05:29 [deepseek-flash] 		var ctype := data.decode_u32(off + 4)
2026-09-11 15:05:29 [deepseek-flash] 		var body := data.slice(off + 8, off + 8 + clen)
2026-09-11 15:05:29 [deepseek-flash] 		if ctype == CHUNK_JSON:
2026-09-11 15:05:29 [deepseek-flash] 			header = JSON.parse_string(body.get_string_from_utf8())
2026-09-11 15:05:29 [deepseek-flash] 		elif ctype == CHUNK_BIN:
2026-09-11 15:05:29 [deepseek-flash] 			binary = body
2026-09-11 15:05:29 [deepseek-flash] 		off += 8 + clen
2026-09-11 15:05:29 [deepseek-flash] 	return {"header": header, "binary": binary}
2026-09-11 15:05:29 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 15:05:29 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 15:05:29 [deepseek-flash] Hook-in
2026-09-11 15:05:29 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 15:05:29 [deepseek-flash] In `pollNetwork`, `get_packet()` gives you a `PackedByteArray` already — you don't have to call
2026-09-11 15:05:29 [deepseek-flash] `get_string_from_utf8()`. So the client loop becomes:
2026-09-11 15:05:29 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 15:05:29 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 15:05:29 [deepseek-flash] var data := client.get_packet()
2026-09-11 15:05:29 [deepseek-flash] if data.size() > 0 and data.decode_u32(0) == FRAME_MAGIC:
2026-09-11 15:05:29 [deepseek-flash] 	var frame := parse_frame(data)
2026-09-11 15:05:29 [deepseek-flash] 	onFrame(client, frame.header, frame.binary)
2026-09-11 15:05:29 [deepseek-flash] else:
2026-09-11 15:05:29 [deepseek-flash] 	onPacket(client, data)   # existing text/JSON path
2026-09-11 15:05:29 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 15:05:29 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 15:05:29 [deepseek-flash] And `onFrame` is a sibling of `onPacket` that dispatches on `header.method`, with the raw bytes
2026-09-11 15:05:29 [deepseek-flash] handed straight to `base64_to_vec2_array`’s replacement — no `Marshalls.base64_to_raw` step.
2026-09-11 15:05:29 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 15:05:29 [deepseek-flash] Notes
2026-09-11 15:05:29 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 15:05:29 [deepseek-flash] - The header chunk is where your `params` live, minus `buffer`. Add `"bin_size"` or a checksum if
2026-09-11 15:05:29 [deepseek-flash] you want integrity checks.
2026-09-11 15:05:29 [deepseek-flash] - `PackedByteArray.decode_u32` is little-endian on all platforms, so no byte-order swap is needed.
2026-09-11 15:05:29 [deepseek-flash] - `slice()` copies; if buffers get large, decode directly out of `data` with an offset instead.
2026-09-11 15:05:29 [deepseek-flash] - If you want to keep base64 for small payloads and only use frames for big ones, gate on
2026-09-11 15:05:29 [deepseek-flash] `header.bin_offset` being present rather than on the magic.
2026-09-11 15:05:29 [deepseek-flash] 
