2026-09-11 15:14:43 [deepseek-flash] Issues
2026-09-11 15:14:43 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 15:14:43 [deepseek-flash] 1. `onFrame` arity mismatch — declared as `func onFrame(client, packet)`, called with three
2026-09-11 15:14:43 [deepseek-flash] args. This will error the moment a frame arrives. Should be `func onFrame(client, header:
2026-09-11 15:14:43 [deepseek-flash] Dictionary, binary: PackedByteArray)`.
2026-09-11 15:14:43 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 15:14:43 [deepseek-flash] 2. `out.fill()` fills the entire buffer — `PackedByteArray.fill()` defaults to `0..size()`.
2026-09-11 15:14:43 [deepseek-flash] Both `out.fill(0x20)` and `out.fill(0x00)` wipe the magic, version, length, and chunk headers you
2026-09-11 15:14:43 [deepseek-flash] just wrote. `fill()` needs explicit ranges: `out.fill(0x20, 20 + json.size(), 20 + json_len)` and
2026-09-11 15:14:43 [deepseek-flash] `out.fill(0x00, 28 + json_len + binary.size(), out.size())`.
2026-09-11 15:14:43 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 15:14:43 [deepseek-flash] 3. JSON body is never copied into `out` — `build_frame` writes the JSON chunk header but
2026-09-11 15:14:43 [deepseek-flash] not `json` itself. Same for the BIN chunk. Simplest fix is to build by concatenation instead of
2026-09-11 15:14:43 [deepseek-flash] pre-sizing and filling:
2026-09-11 15:14:43 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 15:14:43 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 15:14:43 [deepseek-flash]    var out := header_bytes + json + json_pad + bin_header + binary + bin_pad
2026-09-11 15:14:43 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 15:14:43 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 15:14:43 [deepseek-flash] 4. `parse_frame` returns `{}` on bad magic but the caller already guards on magic, so the
2026-09-11 15:14:43 [deepseek-flash] `return {}` path is unreachable from the current call site. Harmless, just dead.
2026-09-11 15:14:43 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 15:14:43 [deepseek-flash] 5. `onFrame` body is empty — expected as a stub, but combined with (1) it will fail on both
2026-09-11 15:14:43 [deepseek-flash] counts.
2026-09-11 15:14:43 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 15:14:43 [deepseek-flash] Want the `onFrame` implementation next, or a corrected `build_frame` first?
