2026-09-11 15:33:45 [deepseek-flash] That’s just missing export templates — Godot doesn’t ship them with the editor. The version in the
2026-09-11 15:33:45 [deepseek-flash] path must match the editor exactly (`4.7.2.stable`), so a template for `4.7.1` or `4.7.3` won’t be
2026-09-11 15:33:45 [deepseek-flash] picked up.
2026-09-11 15:33:45 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 15:33:45 [deepseek-flash] Three ways to fix it:
2026-09-11 15:33:45 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 15:33:45 [deepseek-flash] • 1. Editor (normal path)*
2026-09-11 15:33:45 [deepseek-flash] - `Editor → Manage Export Templates…`
2026-09-11 15:33:45 [deepseek-flash] - Click Download and Install
2026-09-11 15:33:45 [deepseek-flash] - If the download fails or 4.7.2 isn’t listed yet, use option 2.
2026-09-11 15:33:45 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 15:33:45 [deepseek-flash] • 2. Manual install*
2026-09-11 15:33:45 [deepseek-flash] - Grab the matching `.tpz` from https://github.com/godotengine/godot/releases (look for
2026-09-11 15:33:45 [deepseek-flash] `Godot_v4.7.2-stable_export_templates.tpz`).
2026-09-11 15:33:45 [deepseek-flash] - In the same Manage Export Templates dialog, click Install from File… and point it at the
2026-09-11 15:33:45 [deepseek-flash] `.tpz`.
2026-09-11 15:33:45 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 15:33:45 [deepseek-flash] • 3. Manual extraction (if the dialog is uncooperative)*
2026-09-11 15:33:45 [deepseek-flash] - Rename the `.tpz` to `.zip` and extract.
2026-09-11 15:33:45 [deepseek-flash] - You’ll get a `templates/` folder. Copy its contents into:
2026-09-11 15:33:45 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 15:33:45 [deepseek-flash]   C:\Users\nitro\AppData\Roaming\Godot\export_templates\4.7.2.stable\
2026-09-11 15:33:45 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 15:33:45 [deepseek-flash] - The folder should end up containing `windows_debug_x86_64.exe`, `windows_release_x86_64.exe`,
2026-09-11 15:33:45 [deepseek-flash] `version.txt`, etc.
2026-09-11 15:33:45 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 15:33:45 [deepseek-flash] A couple of gotchas worth checking before you chase the download:
2026-09-11 15:33:45 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 15:33:45 [deepseek-flash] - Run `godot --version` (or check Help → About) and confirm it really is `4.7.2.stable`. If it’s
2026-09-11 15:33:45 [deepseek-flash] e.g. `4.7.2.rc1` or `4.7.2.stable.mono`, the template folder name differs.
2026-09-11 15:33:45 [deepseek-flash] - If you’re on the .NET/Mono build, you need the Mono export templates, not the standard ones.
2026-09-11 15:33:45 [deepseek-flash] - The `version.txt` inside the template folder has to say `4.7.2.stable`, otherwise the editor
2026-09-11 15:33:45 [deepseek-flash] silently ignores the whole directory.
2026-09-11 15:33:45 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-11 15:33:45 [deepseek-flash] Once installed, re-open the export dialog; the “No export template found” errors should clear.
2026-09-11 15:33:45 [deepseek-flash] 
