2026-09-11 15:40:00 [grok-build-0.1] Overview
2026-09-11 15:40:00 [grok-build-0.1] This is a Godot relay/host project (`nitrologic`) that bridges Godot with an external
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] system. It runs two roles simultaneously:
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] - Server: TCP port 8080 (accepting WebSocket connections from local clients)
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] - Client: Connects upstream to `ws://localhost:9000`
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] It uses a custom binary framing protocol (`NTRL` magic) that carries a JSON header + optional
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] binary payload.
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] Key Components
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] ╭────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] │  File                          │  Purpose                                                                                                                                                │
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] ├────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] │  `node.gd`                     │  Core networking + protocol logic. Handles frame building/parsing, TCP server, upstream WebSocket, command dispatch (`snoop`, `init`, `draw`, `tick`).  │
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] │  `node2d.gd`                   │  Simple 2D line renderer. Receives `PackedVector2Array` and draws via `draw_multiline`.                                                                 │
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] │  `snoop.gd`                    │  Godot ClassDB introspection. Builds a schema of classes and their methods.                                                                             │
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] │  `control.gd`                  │  Minimal UI host (just prints on ready).                                                                                                                │
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] │  `extension_api.json` snippet  │  Context about `VisualShaderNodeTransformParameter` (uniform mat4).                                                                                     │
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] ╰────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] Notable Design Points
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] • Protocol*
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] - Custom framed format with 4-byte alignment padding.
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] - JSON chunk (`JSON`) + binary chunk (`BIN\0`).
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] - The `onBuffer` path stores binary data by name in a global dictionary (separate from the JSON
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] command path).
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] • Commands currently handled*
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] - `snoop` — triggers schema dump via the Snoop node
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] - `init` — sends splash screen geometry to the Node2D
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] - `draw` — accepts base64-encoded float32 vec2 pairs and updates the line renderer
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] - `tick` — currently just logs
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] • Introspection*
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] The `snoop.gd` implementation walks `ClassDB` and builds a dictionary of class → method names. A
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] lot of the richer metadata (arguments, return types, categories) is currently commented out or only
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] partially populated.
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] Observations
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] 1. Networking is all polled in `_process`. This works but will become noisy as traffic
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] grows. The current split between framed binary and plain text packets is handled reasonably.
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] 2. The `base64_to_vec2_array` function makes a strong assumption about the incoming format (tightly
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] packed float32 pairs). This is fragile if the external side ever changes encoding.
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] 3. The splash screen and draw paths both end up feeding the same `Node2D.set_lines()` method — the
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] architecture is starting to show a "remote drawing" use case.
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] 4. `snoop` currently only emits method names. If the external consumer needs signatures, argument
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] types, or property information, the current schema is quite limited.
2026-09-11 15:40:01 [grok-build-0.1] 
