2026-09-12 07:55:10 [deepseek-flash] I can’t provide DeepSeek’s comments; I’m not that model. Here are my comments on the snippet.
2026-09-12 07:55:10 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-12 07:55:10 [deepseek-flash] 1. Duplicate key
2026-09-12 07:55:10 [deepseek-flash]    `description` appears twice in the same JSON object. JSON does not define reliable behaviour for
2026-09-12 07:55:10 [deepseek-flash] duplicate keys. Many parsers keep the last one, which means your truncated value would overwrite
2026-09-12 07:55:10 [deepseek-flash] the good one.
2026-09-12 07:55:10 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-12 07:55:10 [deepseek-flash] 2. Second value is truncated
2026-09-12 07:55:10 [deepseek-flash]    `"Activist software developer knee deep in RSS and open syste`
2026-09-12 07:55:10 [deepseek-flash]    is missing `ms"` at the end. As written, that would make the JSON invalid.
2026-09-12 07:55:10 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-12 07:55:10 [deepseek-flash] 3. Keep the complete value
2026-09-12 07:55:10 [deepseek-flash]    The first line is the one to keep:
2026-09-12 07:55:10 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-12 07:55:10 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-12 07:55:10 [deepseek-flash]    "description": "Activist software developer knee deep in RSS and open systems"
2026-09-12 07:55:10 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-12 07:55:10 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-12 07:55:10 [deepseek-flash] 4. Remove the duplicate
2026-09-12 07:55:10 [deepseek-flash]    Do not include both. If the corrected line is followed by another member, keep the trailing
2026-09-12 07:55:10 [deepseek-flash] comma; otherwise remove it.
2026-09-12 07:55:10 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-12 07:55:10 [deepseek-flash] 5. Comments in JSON
2026-09-12 07:55:10 [deepseek-flash]    Standard JSON does not support comments. If you need annotation, use a separate field such as
2026-09-12 07:55:10 [deepseek-flash] `_comment` or keep notes outside the file.
2026-09-12 07:55:10 [deepseek-flash] 
