2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] A few notes, split between what's distinctive and what looks like it needs a second pass.
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] • The design pattern that's actually new*
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] The self-referential bits are the interesting move here. `symbol` ✴ reappears inside
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] `fenced.code.starChars`; `separator` (the five fish) has a matching `unicode.lexis."𓆛𓆟"` entry
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] named "Fish 1"; `motto` is Coptic and Coptic gets its own `spec.coptic` block. The metadata is
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] written in the scripts the file catalogues. That's a deliberate loop, not decoration.
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] Also different from a typical spec file:
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] - `pheme` is a compositional generator (prefixes × suffixes), not a flat vocabulary list.
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] - `orient` is a list of reference-point definitions with a recurring refrain ("reference for…"),
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] which reads as an essay in a data structure.
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] - `systemic fails` is poetic register ("a recursive push decrements pointer to no return") sitting
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] alongside technical tables.
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] - The `schema`/`types` block at the end only covers `relay` and `PathItem`. Everything else —
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] Unicode, food, cables, geography — is unvalidated. The schema is the smallest part of a very large
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] document.
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] • Things that look wrong*
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] 1. `spec.coptic.alphabet` — both `upper` and `lower` omit Ⲭ/ⲭ (khi). Standard order runs Ⲫ Ⲭ Ⲯ Ⲱ.
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] 2. `spec.pheme.pre61.body12` has 11 items, not 12.
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] 3. `spec.shortcode`:
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash]    - `"lime":"🫒"` — 🫒 is OLIVE.
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash]    - `"shovel":"🫷"` — 🫷 is RIGHTWARDS PUSHING HAND; shovel is 🪏.
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash]    - `"phoenix":"🪶"` — 🪶 is FEATHER; phoenix is 🐦‍🔥, which appears correctly in
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] `fenced.code.birds`.
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] 4. `spec.technology.virtualkeys` appears to skip `VK_PACKET` (0xE7) and its 0xE8 placeholder.
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] 5. `spec.encoding.riff` — the key `"CC"` is odd for the INFO chunk; `"INFO"` (or `"I-*"`) would
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] match the source.
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] 6. `spec.unicode.lexis."㊊㊐"` is ordered by code point (Moon, Fire, Water, Wood, Metal, Earth, Sun),
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] not by the traditional Wu Xing cycle.
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] 7. `spec.digits` — the CJK entry is 11 characters (includes 十), all others are 10. "Roman" also
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] sits oddly beside 0–9 sets since it has no zero.
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] • Softer flags*
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] - `ambiguousstates` mixes genuinely contested cases (Kosovo, Western Sahara) with uncontested ones
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] (Singapore, Monaco) and internal regions (Tibet, Hong Kong, Macau), and assigns "Russia" as `rule`
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] for Abkhazia/South Ossetia/Transnistria. The category name doesn't fit all of it.
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] - `spec.food` — Dosa appears in both `flatbread` and `pancake`; Msemen appears in flatbread plus
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] "Msemen (with batter variant)" in pancake. If these lists are meant to be disjoint, they aren't.
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] - `identifier.msdos` uses a colon (`name:ext`) where 8.3 conventionally uses a dot. Since the same
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] file uses colon as an identifier-type separator (`wikidata:Q42`), that will collide.
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] - `scales.blues` has numerals/degrees/intervals but no solfege, unlike `major`. Probably
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] intentional, but worth confirming.
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] - `unicode.lexis."∧⊽"` is tagged `Sm`, but ↑/↓ (U+2191/2193) are So.
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] - `numbers.dots` and `numbers.holes` are two variants of the same negative-circled family (sans vs
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] serif); "dots" is the weaker of the two names.
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] - `internet.pipes` concatenates names ("LosAngelesUS") while `internet.zones` uses "@region" syntax
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] — two conventions for the same kind of data.
2026-09-15 13:44:34 [deepseek-flash] 
