2026-09-15 13:59:44 [deepseek-flash] into the sibling `maze` repo. Only the first two change together; the dumps don't.
2026-09-15 13:59:44 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-15 13:59:44 [deepseek-flash] • The idea worth keeping* is the pairing in `archaic.md` — RFC 2119 keywords beside the
2026-09-15 13:59:44 [deepseek-flash] Early Modern English verb table. "SHALL" in a standards document is the same modal as "shall" in a
2026-09-15 13:59:44 [deepseek-flash] legal instrument, and the file says so by juxtaposition rather than by explaining it. The
2026-09-15 13:59:44 [deepseek-flash] `codepoint_card` then extends it: `SHALL_TRUNCATE`, `shall_render`. That's RFC 2119 language used
2026-09-15 13:59:44 [deepseek-flash] as a UI assertion vocabulary, and it's coherent.
2026-09-15 13:59:44 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-15 13:59:45 [deepseek-flash] Two fixes there:
2026-09-15 13:59:45 [deepseek-flash] - The first JSON block is missing a comma after the closing `]` of `RFC2119keywords`.
2026-09-15 13:59:45 [deepseek-flash] - Casing is split — `shall_render` / `shall_clip` / `shall_center` (lowercase keys) against
2026-09-15 13:59:45 [deepseek-flash] `SHALL_TRUNCATE` / `SHALL_HIGHLIGHT` (uppercase values). If the rule is "lowercase boolean flag,
2026-09-15 13:59:45 [deepseek-flash] uppercase enumerated assertion", state it once; otherwise it reads as drift.
2026-09-15 13:59:45 [deepseek-flash] - RFC 2119 spells them with spaces, not underscores (`MUST NOT`, `SHALL NOT`, `NOT RECOMMENDED`).
2026-09-15 13:59:45 [deepseek-flash] Underscores are fine for a schema but won't match spec text if anything is ever compared.
2026-09-15 13:59:45 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-15 13:59:45 [deepseek-flash] • `bibli.js` — one real bug, several latent:*
2026-09-15 13:59:45 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-15 13:59:45 [deepseek-flash] - `if((appWidth!=cols)||(appHeight|=rows))` — `|=` is bitwise-OR-assign; it should be `!=`. As
2026-09-15 13:59:45 [deepseek-flash] written, `appHeight` is corrupted on every resize and the branch fires almost always.
2026-09-15 13:59:45 [deepseek-flash] - `link`, `close`, `url`, `alphaStyles` are implicit globals. Fine in a classic `<script>`, fatal
2026-09-15 13:59:45 [deepseek-flash] the moment you add `type="module"` — which the file's own TODO anticipates.
2026-09-15 13:59:45 [deepseek-flash] - The `for(const alpha of alphabet)` loop computes `alphaStyles` and discards it. That's leftover
2026-09-15 13:59:45 [deepseek-flash] from the CSS-property exploration visible in `notes.txt`.
2026-09-15 13:59:45 [deepseek-flash] - `emit` writes via `innerHTML` and builds anchors by string concatenation, so a `"` or `<` inside
